            <ArticleTitle>[Sclerotherapy with Betadine for simple cysts of the kidney. Apropos of 7 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>237-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report on 7 cases of benign, symptomatic renal cysts treated by percutaneous sclerosis using Betadine solution. The mean size of the cysts was 8 cm and we obtained progressive collapse of all of them. This technique was a simple and effective methode with good results. Indeed, 85% of the cysts disappeard, and only one patient retained a small asymptomatic residual cavity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
